"lines": [
"November fourteenth, 2004. Off southern California, four Navy flyers are sent to check something strange.",
"For a week, radar on the USS Princeton had tracked objects that operators said dropped from eighty thousand feet in seconds.",
"Commander David Fravor and Lieutenant Commander Alex Dietrich, each with a backseat officer, find whitewater churning over the ocean.",
"Above it hovers a small white object. Forty feet long. No wings. No exhaust.",
"Fravor spirals down to look. The object turns, and mirrors him, rising to meet his jet.",
"Then it leaves. Another jet films it on infrared. The Pentagon released that video in twenty twenty, calling it unidentified.",
"Skeptics point to glare, parallax, even sensor errors.",
"Four trained flyers watched it for five minutes.",
"Misread sensors, or something that mirrored a fighter jet?"
